  "event_layout": "Call opcode, six argument words, then state before scripted mutations. Path arguments are unit, source row, target row, source column, opaque unit-index carry and target column. Execute arguments are unit, animation request, raw uint8 column, opaque unit-index carry and finite double low/high words. Panel observes unit-index carry. Free common arguments are zero; original pointer/EDX and native no-argument checks are separate.",
  "final_layout": "Raw function result, state, then FNV-1a32 fingerprints of both full arenas and the path source. Per-state queued-path values are also FNV-1a32 fingerprints. These fingerprints are not literal full-byte comparisons.",
  "copy_check": "Independently at the free boundary, both recorders compare the entire two-arena byte buffers against copies captured after the path boundary mutations with exactly 404 destination bytes replaced. This directly checks all copy bytes and every untouched arena byte, including adjacent guards, for this bounded storage.",
  "animation_evidence": "Original MOV EDX,1 at 0x424F3F precedes REP MOVSD. The 0x461C70 free wrapper jumps to _nfree_0x4740DD, which pushes EDX at 0x4740DF and restores it at 0x4741DD on every returning path. The executor at 0x410330 saves and uses EDX. Native animate=1 repairs the old uninitialized v9; it requests animation that the real executor can later disable.",
  "neighbor_projection": "Original 64 contiguous DWORDs at 0x513334 overlap DY starting four bytes later. Native DX[64] and DY[63] are separate arrays; actual initializers are extracted and checked. The common state projects DX[2*d],DY[2*d] for backed d=0..31. Scripted physical-word mutations explicitly update both corresponding native views; all 127 native elements are independently checked. This is no production alias repair or general alias-equivalence claim.",
  "before_comparison": "All 89 defined null-path before cases match original/after in four profiles. The other 141 cases are excluded before: 133 success paths read uninitialized v9, and eight additional null paths overflow signed coordinate addition. There are 16 coordinate-overflow cases total, eight already within the success exclusion. Original-after is primary for the repairs; no patched-before success oracle is used.",
  "compile_diagnostic_policy": "Actual-after recorder uses Wall/Wextra/Werror and UBSan with the packed-layout alignment exception. No diagnostic exception is needed for the repaired body.",
  "evidence": "artifacts/readability/road-functions-20260906/batch-13/original-proof/ and test-audit/ (private evidence; public tests require only tracked code and fixtures)",
  "limits": [
    "Four callee entries are scripted recording/mutation boundaries. The original helper instructions and actual native helper body execute, but pathfinding, allocator behavior, movement gameplay and rendering do not.",
    "Original path uses RET4 and the original free boundary observes EAX path identity plus preserved EDX=1. Native free remains a no-argument inert compatibility boundary. Scripted ignored return values do not redefine actual callees.",
    "The opaque EBP value forwarded to path/executor/panel here is unitIndex. It is not renamed as action points or replaced with the 725-byte offset. Original carried registers are explicitly preserved at adapters; complete real callee register behavior is outside this boundary proof.",
    "Native pointer identities are validated separately from raw integer return observations. All storage is valid, backed, positive signed-low32; path source and destination do not overlap. Original forward REP MOVSD is not claimed equivalent to native memcpy on overlapping ranges.",
    "Finite double bits, including signed zero, subnormals and finite extremes, are forwarded exactly. No NaN, infinity or floating-point environment claim is made. Native char forwarding compares its raw low byte.",
    "All 32 indices fit both native neighbor arrays; only the first eight are named gameplay directions. Negative or out-of-bounds directions and invalid stack indices are excluded without inventing clamps or fallback results.",
    "No retail assets, runtime route, visual comparison or campaign milestone is established by these fixtures."
  ]
